Description: Add sw64 (Sunway) architecture support
 The vendored target-lexicon and libc crates do not know the sw64
 architecture, so building librsvg on sw64 (Sunway) machines fails in the
 target-lexicon build script with:
 .
   Invalid target name: 'sw_64-sunway-linux-gnu'
 .
 Teach target-lexicon about sw64, port the sw64 definitions of libc (from the
 UOS rust-libc 0.2.155 package) into the vendored libc 0.2.153, and add the
 sw64 modules and target_arch = "sw64" arms to the vendored linux-raw-sys
 0.4.13 (from the UOS rust-linux-raw-sys 0.4.12 package).  linux-raw-sys is
 reached through rustix, which criterion and tempfile pull in, so without it
 `make check` fails with:
 .
   error[E0432]: unresolved import `crate::general`
 .
 All three vendor checksums are refreshed.
 .
 Not listed in debian/patches/series on purpose: dpkg-source refuses quilt
 patches that modify the debian directory ("Reversed (or previously applied)
 patch detected").  debian/rules applies this patch instead.
Author: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
